        "problem": "$\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x-{150}^{\u2218})=$",
        "worked_solution": "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={150}^{\u2218},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x-{150}^{\u2218}) & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{150}^{\u2218}-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{150}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
